  "description": "T6 Magnolia (Magnolia spp.), Rear Garden\r\nProposed works:\r\nReduce overall crown size by approximately 1.5–2 metres in height and lateral spread\r\nLight crown lift to remove low lateral growth (sporeas) from 5 metres to approx. 3–4 metres\r\nRemove any crossing or congested branches as part of routine pruning and clearance\r\nCurrent dimensions: Approx. 5 metres in height, 5 metres in radial spread\r\nFinished dimensions: Approx. 3–4 metres in height, 3–4 metres in radial spread\r\n\r\nJustification:\r\nRoutine maintenance to manage size in proportion to garden space\r\nImprove access and shape by removing low lateral growth\r\nPromote balanced, healthy crown structure and reduce density\r\nEnhance ornamental value and long-term vitality of the tree\r\n\r\nCompliance:\r\nAll pruning works to be completed in accordance with BS 3998:2010 – Recommendations for Tree Work, ensuring clean cuts to appropriate secondary growth points to maintain the tree’s health and natural form",
